  contentsAnswer: Workshop tools and padding. I am repairing a truck tomorrow.
  weightAnswer: Nearly fifteen kilos with the hard case. Yes, it is heavy.
  metalAnswer: Steel spanners, sockets and a hammer; a strong metal response is expected.
  packingAnswer: The tray is not latched; it can slide a little downhill.
  responseAnswer: A short metal rattle. Once the tray settles, it should stay on
    that side.
  authorReasoning: Heavy and metal-rich is legitimate. Tilt shifts downhill; leveling
    preserves tray displacement. No active recovery.
